First Nations Tax (FNT) Schedule
Do not use this area. Fill out this schedule if you are required to collect the First Nations tax and you sell alcoholic 
beverages, fuel, and/or tobacco products (listed products) from a location on a reserve. Use it to 
separately show the amounts of GST/HST and FNT that you must report on your GST/HST return. 
You are required to file both of the following for each reporting period:
•Form GST34-2, Goods and Services Tax/Harmonized Sales Tax (GST/HST) Return for Registrants
(or Form GST62, non-personalized version)
•Form GST499-1, First Nations Tax (FNT) Schedule
If you file your GST/HST return electronically, send your FNT schedule separately by mail no later than the due date of 
your GST/HST return. The reporting period and the due date for the FNT schedule will be the same as for your GST/HST return. 
You have to file them together.
Notes 
For reporting periods that begin after December 2023, all GST/HST registrants, with the exception of charities and selected 
listed financial institutions (SLFIs), are required to file GST/HST returns electronically.
You, or your authorized representative, have to sign the schedule and file it with your GST/HST return. You must keep copies 
of all documents to support your net tax calculations for audit purposes.
For more information, see page 4.
